      "20": {
        "attributes": {
          "alignment": {
            "type": "integer",
            "value": 0
          },
          "fill": {
            "type": "bool",
            "value": false
          },
          "font-size": {
            "type": "float",
            "value": 19
          },
          "text": {
            "type": "string",
            "value": "TRANSFORMATION 2D EXAMPLE\n\nIn this example we have two Transformation2D nodes, one for the Mesh2D node and one for the Camera2D node.\nThe first  Transformation2D node gets its translation data from a Linear node(for x) and Sine node(for y).\nIt also gets scale data from the Scale slider (a float in node).\n\nThe second Transformation2D node gets all its information from sliders (Float In nodes).\nBy working like this, the first Transformation2D node gives us control over the individual meshes.\nAnd the second Transformation2D nodes gives us control over the entire rendered mesh.\nThe second Transformation2D also makes sure we don't need a regular Transform node after we've already rendered the meshes."
          }
        },
        "bounds": {
          "height": 713.2225341796875,
          "width": 2380.985107421875,
          "x": -351.7930908203125,
          "y": 225.5894317626953
